    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="1012" n="1000" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg1000"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/5–1145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Truman to the Acting Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and the Foreign Economic
                        Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crowley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-11">May 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I approve the policy of lend-lease supplies to the U.S.S.R. recommended in your
                    memorandum of May 11, 1945. In carrying out the policy, you should, until
                    further notice, proceed on the assumption that the U.S.S.R. will enter into the
                    war against Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Truman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
